// HZM coop - SITUATIONAL AI VOICE pools (coop_mod/aivoice.scr).
//
// One alias name per (nationality, situation). Multiple entries under the same alias name
// are a RANDOM-VARIANT SET in the engine alias table (Alias_ListFindRandom), so the driver
// just plays the situation name and the engine rolls a line.
//
// Every pool below is drawn from the retail generic soldier VO, grouped by the ORIGINAL
// authoring taxonomy so the meaning always matches the trigger:
//   Alt_ = alert/spotted   Sig_ = direction call   Cov_ = take cover   Grn_ = grenade!
//   Ret_ = fall back       Ang_ = angry taunt      Vic_ = kill/victory  Atk_ = press attack
//   dfr_sighted/cover/panic/kill/attack = the American equivalents
// Nationality is picked from the ACTOR MODEL by coop_mod/aivoice.scr (de/it/us/uk), never
// from team alone - British models get DFRUK lines, US models never do.
//
// Scoped to every coop map family so the pools work on AA (m), Spearhead (t) and
// Breakthrough (e) alike - the retail per-map alias scoping is what left t/e maps silent.
// Played with `<actor> playsound <alias>` so the sound is emitted BY THE ACTOR ENTITY and
// is distance attenuated. WAV pools use `loaded` (true 3D path); the BT/SH reels are mp3
// and the engine always plays mp3 2D, so those stay entity-attached stereo with falloff.

// coop_av_de_contact
alias coop_av_de_contact sound/dialogue/generic/g/sighted/alt_g_001b.wav soundparms 1.15 0.10 1.0 0.05 220 2400 dialog loaded maps "m e t dm obj train"
alias coop_av_de_contact sound/dialogue/generic/g/sighted/alt_g_001e.wav soundparms 1.15 0.10 1.0 0.05 220 2400 dialog loaded maps "m e t dm obj train"
